        "quote": "The nonresidential design standards in this chapter are intended to provide a minimum level of acceptable design for nonresidential development projects. The design standards establish basic requirements for development of buildings and their architectural components, which are common to all types of commercial development. The design standards are not intended to promote a particular style of architecture or design theme but will enable developers, architects, landowners and the general public to anticipate and plan for building design as a key element of the overall project approval process. The standards accomplish the following objectives:",
